# Insurance.svg and INSURANCE.svg are two files on the live host differing only
# in filename case -- the same artwork at a 60x60 and an 80x80 viewBox (every
# coordinate scales by 4/3: 35.625 -> 47.5, 6.875 -> 9.16667). NTFS cannot hold
# both names in one directory, so the mirror stores the uppercase file and sends
# the lowercase URL to it. SVG scales and the rendered size is set in CSS, so
# they are visually interchangeable. Without this, the three pages that
# reference the lowercase name lose the icon on any case-sensitive host --
# which is every Linux and macOS checkout, and most static hosts.
/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Insurance.svg  /wp-content/uploads/2023/12/INSURANCE.svg        301

